{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"5e959f56-db87-43d9-969f-1b5ab4879505","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/deterministic-request-entrance/review-feedback-002.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":true,"findings":[{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"tests/unit/architecture/request-entrance-llm-boundary.test.ts","title":"B-18 regression guard tests are trivially true — grepE never called","rationale":"The 'B-18 regression guard' describe block (lines 107–135) contains two tests that assert `expect(syntheticMatch).not.toBe(\"\")` where `syntheticMatch` is a hardcoded non-empty string literal. These tests always pass and do not call grepE, so they do not actually validate the detection mechanism. The real B-18 protection (the grepE-based tests in the first two describe blocks) IS functional — adding a forbidden import to src/core/request/ or src/core/command/request-*.ts would cause those tests to fail. The regression guard section is misleading but does not undermine core protection.","line":107},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"tests/unit/generate-chain-removed.test.ts","title":"Duplicate test file: generate-chain-removed.test.ts mirrors deprecated-generate-removal.test.ts","rationale":"tests/unit/generate-chain-removed.test.ts (291 lines) and tests/unit/cli/deprecated-generate-removal.test.ts (291 lines) cover TC-005, TC-007, TC-008, TC-009, TC-010, TC-011, TC-012, TC-014, TC-016 with essentially equivalent assertions. Both files were added in this change. This doubles maintenance burden (~291 lines) without adding any additional coverage. One of the two files should be removed."}],"evidence":{"checked":17,"skipped":0,"unverified":1},"observations":[]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-07-31T02:56:49.141Z","endedAt":"2026-07-31T03:02:11.315Z","commitOid":"dfc2e5db0e89c4b88a707e4